Reason: the tile-skip grid (patch 0065) was built again over every tile of the room whenever the tile-order version
moved: ~10.5 ms on the real Wii for rm_a3h04's ~4,800 tiles, on two of every three frames while its sand crumbles.
Its cells now count ranks from their depth's run, so tile_add, tile_delete and tile_set_scale edit the grid in place
when it and the tile run (patch 0077) were current before the edit: a new tile takes the next rank of its depth's run
(a new depth gets a run without cells) and goes into the cells its box covers, or among the always visited when those
cells leave the grid; a deleted tile leaves every cell and the later ranks of its run move down one; a rescaled tile
moves to its new cells. A run with more than 256 always visited tiles, and any other tile edit, gets a full grid again.
Every tile the renderer would draw is still visited, in draw order.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

